## 3. Keep every consuming component working unchanged: the `useBotGraph` selector

Dozens of existing components read `bot.nodes`/`bot.edges` directly and were written against that shape — the builder page, `GraphThumbnail`, `OverviewTab`, the My Presets cards, the Compare page from Phase 5, all of it. Don't touch any of them. Instead, add one selector hook that reconstructs the old shape on demand:

```
export function useBotGraph(botId: string | undefined) {
  return useWorkspace((s) => {
    if (!botId) return { nodes: [] as BotNode[], edges: [] as BotEdge[] }
    const idx = s.graphIndex[botId]
    if (!idx) return { nodes: [], edges: [] }
    return {
      nodes: idx.nodeIds.map((id) => s.nodesById[id]),
      edges: idx.edgeIds.map((id) => s.edgesById[id]),
    }
  })
}
```

Then do a find-and-replace across the codebase: everywhere a component currently does `const bot = useBot(botId)` and then reads `bot.nodes`/`bot.edges`, keep the `useBot(botId)` call for metadata (rename its return type to `BotMeta`, everything else about it stays the same) and add `const { nodes, edges } = useBotGraph(botId)` alongside it for graph data. This is a mechanical, low-risk change precisely because you're preserving the exact `{ nodes, edges }` shape everything already expects — the normalization happens underneath, not in every call site.

